Subject: Block on final Vulkan fences instead of polling on the host
Base: llama.cpp a34de8618b25dfc32ee43749db47d767a9f0a25d (b12015)

Why: upstream PR #12630 introduced hybrid sleeping/polling to reduce fence
wake-up latency (up to 5% higher throughput on NVIDIA/Windows):
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/12630

A resident assistant favors lower CPU consumption. The final polling loop
accounted for 16.96% of sampled process CPU time in a user-supplied Vulkan
profile. Wait on the same final fence using Vulkan's blocking API. Keep the
intermediate fence lifecycle, final reset ordering, and VK_CHECK device-loss
reporting/error propagation. No submission, ABI, or public API changes.

